[[:db/retract 17592186052277 :answer-field/choices 17592186052278] [:db/retract 17592186052277 :answer-field/choices 17592186052279] [:db/retract 17592186052277 :answer-field/choices 17592186052280] [:db/retract 17592186052277 :answer-field/choices 17592186052281] [:db/retract 17592186052277 :answer-field/choices 17592186052282] {:db/id 17592186054720 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a174f7c-09d0-50e5-afac-66bf0cc4c315"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054486 :question/worked-solution "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In a downwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the maximum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(-2,3).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=-2.$\n\n![](images/91/91e9d323945b1520aa36b70f3faf8c801e28b21437cd1008b54e76dae76d5ccb.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1834012f-4a0b-5e03-8f32-bee5b9948e5b" "question-8a08fd8f-f28b-522d-892c-2595551ed22c" "question-d8dc19dd-4912-57fc-b7e0-84c553fa7c79" "question-ba657a54-9357-5409-90cb-ee552f02dde2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054487 :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola. \n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-2,0)$ and $(4,0).$ \n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1100bf2f-961a-5344-8257-63842e33b322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054578 :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e012ecda75df732e1c96ea4a52762fb085f444f41991ed9a3fe72d7d8e10025.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y=x^2+2x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+2x+k \\\\ y & =(0)^{2}+2(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=0$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $\\left(0,0\\right).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-53ebdab8-abca-5063-be77-653bbbd15d1e" "question-57d98e6f-6b53-5ed4-abd4-c02ceb5b88f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054488 :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=-x^2+4x-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=-x^2+4x-3.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=0,1,2,3,4$ and then use the formula $y=-x^2+4x-3$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-3$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/44/442d3550eb77f837da6875bc3877023db44f9f3ee862b433fa56d2186c352bd2.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/e9/e95ebb53e7924dc1e99a92be85e6981def3c1186029c6c620bded4bb797f0c06.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055158 :question/worked-solution "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In an upwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the minimum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(3,-2).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=3.$\n\n![](images/f1/f139192260875d5e988f30a64a7024f50d68337dbd4969d938f18aa62b850dd0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186052277 :answer-field/correct "answer-890cbcbb-a92b-5d7c-8d74-969403bf22bd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f277e75-74ce-54d2-9035-15a37f995d14" "answer-4d276868-fe6b-507d-8ab9-43180ad9fccc" "answer-c8731d7b-9b13-5a37-a523-9ea5e0ef05e7" "answer-890cbcbb-a92b-5d7c-8d74-969403bf22bd" "answer-cd58fa58-4a48-5b20-a716-a9639b6de6ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f277e75-74ce-54d2-9035-15a37f995d14" :answer/id #uuid "4f277e75-74ce-54d2-9035-15a37f995d14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(-2,3)$, line of symmetry: $y=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d276868-fe6b-507d-8ab9-43180ad9fccc" :answer/id #uuid "4d276868-fe6b-507d-8ab9-43180ad9fccc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(2,3)$, line of symmetry: $x=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8731d7b-9b13-5a37-a523-9ea5e0ef05e7" :answer/id #uuid "c8731d7b-9b13-5a37-a523-9ea5e0ef05e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(3,-2)$, line of symmetry: $x=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-890cbcbb-a92b-5d7c-8d74-969403bf22bd" :answer/id #uuid "890cbcbb-a92b-5d7c-8d74-969403bf22bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(3,-2)$, line of symmetry: $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd58fa58-4a48-5b20-a716-a9639b6de6ec" :answer/id #uuid "cd58fa58-4a48-5b20-a716-a9639b6de6ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(3,2)$, line of symmetry: $y=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a174f7c-09d0-50e5-afac-66bf0cc4c315" :question/id #uuid "5a174f7c-09d0-50e5-afac-66bf0cc4c315" :question/math-academy-id "q-106029" :question/problem "![](images/68/687ea4a6fac8c4c6b7df7336f13b8ca39eb1b7049990c9875eeeaf556bd5353c.png)\n\nFor the parabola shown above, find the vertex and the equation of the axis of symmetry." :question/worked-solution "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In an upwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the maximum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(5,6).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=5.$\n\n![](images/ed/ed00e2896127e6f3da7fc8e63c22e1944434060ac53e4e63d31f1cd7590a8627.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e979b5aa-d854-5946-b2f2-b44451a4405d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e979b5aa-d854-5946-b2f2-b44451a4405d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e979b5aa-d854-5946-b2f2-b44451a4405d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-20a1c38f-14d0-54c2-aa1b-27992356d597" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5be5250d-98eb-544c-bd07-c52401dbba56" "answer-20a1c38f-14d0-54c2-aa1b-27992356d597" "answer-49182a1a-d1a2-5516-844d-c2cbd63c579b" "answer-8aa5f12a-3886-539c-b393-38d2c6a11432" "answer-179ea49a-2fe6-598c-98e3-82ebaa8f23c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5be5250d-98eb-544c-bd07-c52401dbba56" :answer/id #uuid "5be5250d-98eb-544c-bd07-c52401dbba56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(5,-6)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20a1c38f-14d0-54c2-aa1b-27992356d597" :answer/id #uuid "20a1c38f-14d0-54c2-aa1b-27992356d597" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(5,6)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49182a1a-d1a2-5516-844d-c2cbd63c579b" :answer/id #uuid "49182a1a-d1a2-5516-844d-c2cbd63c579b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(5,6)$, line of symmetry: $x=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8aa5f12a-3886-539c-b393-38d2c6a11432" :answer/id #uuid "8aa5f12a-3886-539c-b393-38d2c6a11432" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(6,5)$, line of symmetry: $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-179ea49a-2fe6-598c-98e3-82ebaa8f23c6" :answer/id #uuid "179ea49a-2fe6-598c-98e3-82ebaa8f23c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "vertex: $(6,5)$, line of symmetry: $x=6$" :db/ensure [:an