/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb89a373-134a-511e-bb9e-a5f83a1aa2b8" :answer/id #uuid "fb89a373-134a-511e-bb9e-a5f83a1aa2b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f04964f-2301-566c-83e7-ae340242fcf2" :answer/id #uuid "5f04964f-2301-566c-83e7-ae340242fcf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0079827-2b4a-51cb-9347-a6b433588055" :answer/id #uuid "a0079827-2b4a-51cb-9347-a6b433588055" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234449 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a36c5be-bb58-5992-90d2-1b9b6c33f67b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a36c5be-bb58-5992-90d2-1b9b6c33f67b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a36c5be-bb58-5992-90d2-1b9b6c33f67b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-780a86b0-806e-5172-9848-d1df1932bb7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80de2eb0-6caf-5df9-8c58-692b1d2bc75b" "answer-165ecd6b-2ac4-5fd1-8c73-a2644c7f185d" "answer-c0ce0898-747d-5c52-bd5f-3c34f462a124" "answer-780a86b0-806e-5172-9848-d1df1932bb7b" "answer-ca5c6042-a815-5608-beed-8a21ca8c1365"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80de2eb0-6caf-5df9-8c58-692b1d2bc75b" :answer/id #uuid "80de2eb0-6caf-5df9-8c58-692b1d2bc75b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-165ecd6b-2ac4-5fd1-8c73-a2644c7f185d" :answer/id #uuid "165ecd6b-2ac4-5fd1-8c73-a2644c7f185d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0ce0898-747d-5c52-bd5f-3c34f462a124" :answer/id #uuid "c0ce0898-747d-5c52-bd5f-3c34f462a124" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-780a86b0-806e-5172-9848-d1df1932bb7b" :answer/id #uuid "780a86b0-806e-5172-9848-d1df1932bb7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca5c6042-a815-5608-beed-8a21ca8c1365" :answer/id #uuid "ca5c6042-a815-5608-beed-8a21ca8c1365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1100bf2f-961a-5344-8257-63842e33b322" :question/id #uuid "1100bf2f-961a-5344-8257-63842e33b322" :question/math-academy-id "q-106044" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cf3840cca56d90bc6b3981d15ead9c4ae45665693ef5c7794e65574204e632db.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y={x}^{2}-3x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-3x+k \\\\ y & =(0)^{2}-3(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we see that we must have $k=2$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36426514-7bc1-54d9-8654-f61d7bab9bb8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36426514-7bc1-54d9-8654-f61d7bab9bb8" :answer-field/id #uuid "36426514-7bc1-54d9-8654-f61d7bab9bb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9aab5299-31bb-531a-9577-a930edf4db8d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-654e1f9b-f174-5aa1-910d-781435311218" "answer-46525a5c-083e-57ca-a9c6-230718510f4d" "answer-9811c8d3-c957-52fb-9b1d-e16c0bfa96be" "answer-0ac7d6e1-050b-59bb-8459-6b9fce755995" "answer-9aab5299-31bb-531a-9577-a930edf4db8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-654e1f9b-f174-5aa1-910d-781435311218" :answer/id #uuid "654e1f9b-f174-5aa1-910d-781435311218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46525a5c-083e-57ca-a9c6-230718510f4d" :answer/id #uuid "46525a5c-083e-57ca-a9c6-230718510f4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9811c8d3-c957-52fb-9b1d-e16c0bfa96be" :answer/id #uuid "9811c8d3-c957-52fb-9b1d-e16c0bfa96be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ac7d6e1-050b-59bb-8459-6b9fce755995" :answer/id #uuid "0ac7d6e1-050b-59bb-8459-6b9fce755995" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aab5299-31bb-531a-9577-a930edf4db8d" :answer/id #uuid "9aab5299-31bb-531a-9577-a930edf4db8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-53ebdab8-abca-5063-be77-653bbbd15d1e" :question/id #uuid "53ebdab8-abca-5063-be77-653bbbd15d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106057" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,$ and then use the formula $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $3$ | $13$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/b4/b43e0f6b6f359b08dd346a30509d82482a3b82defac90728ddaa7c9769690846.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/8d/8de7d3c268e35f85da8f1bf7882d2ebd285fa3f5c0c239c986eeb1564277e4e1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb700264-272d-54a5-aa96-05b215519e4b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb700264-272d-54a5-aa96-05b215519e4b" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb700264-272d-54a5-aa96-05b215519e4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56f9ea1a-984f-5c8f-9d69-f76de09e5137" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa8f322d-12cf-527b-9535-e15eef757d1f" "answer-6ba4edf5-3a2e-5873-bbde-115b6a4cb0b1" "answer-52d72a9e-8d18-5223-88c1-28fe8f4dfaac" "answer-56f9ea1a-984f-5c8f-9d69-f76de09e5137" "answer-275c3b78-1f78-5062-a1b1-5603932f8c55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa8f322d-12cf-527b-9535-e15eef757d1f" :answer/id #uuid "fa8f322d-12cf-527b-9535-e15eef757d1f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/62/622f81fb3304e6300fa0c82d8c540685268e9fde56c8a6e986edc3f788ef54db.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ba4edf5-3a2e-5873-bbde-115b6a4cb0b1" :answer/id #uuid "6ba4edf5-3a2e-5873-bbde-115b6a4cb0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/6d/6d5eaff1bbe70dc963ca08e2bfddeab05d8dbd61df68fe85f3545ee979d969be.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52d72a9e-8d18-5223-88c1-28fe8f4dfaac" :answer/id #uuid "52d72a9e-8d18-5223-88c1-28fe8f4dfaac" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/75/7575e4eaecb7e5a84397b0a0a9b9661f6f83db71a0304c2e2e31e3ab42ec801d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56f9ea1a-984f-5c8f-9d69-f76de09e5137" :answer/id #uuid "56f9ea1a-984f-5c8f-9d69-f76de09e5137" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8d/8de7d3c268e35f85da8f1bf7882d2ebd285fa3f5c0c239c986eeb1564277e4e1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-275c3b78-1f78-5062-a1b1-5603932f8c55" :answer/id #uuid "275c3b78-1f78-5062-a1b1-5603932f8c55" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b9/b9a8459c307939f7b95290217f8d98ce23a1e9317706adf8e5c4761d225e34ab.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-57d98e6f-6b53-5ed4-abd4-c02ceb5b88f3" :question/id #uuid "57d98e6f-6b53-5ed4-abd4-c02ceb5b88f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-106054" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y=-{x}^{2}+10x-28?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=-{x}^{2}+10x-28.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=3,4,5,6,7,8,$ and then use the formula $y=-{x}^{2}+10x-28$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $-7$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-7$ | $-12$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/b7/b762d214dbd72555b069846ca8e7bcb5248c73c15db10f06018167ff7966d6d0.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/24/24aae5c27fc48b7a340e36f6a54d9d6d636644c938e5328c1a8c68713179a947.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d4c217e0-5a36-5f19-a946-f15d4311ad3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d4c217e0-5a36-5f19-a946-f15d4311ad3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c217e0-5a36-5f19-a946-f15d4311ad3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7a9cd5f1-cfb7-5a25-b73f-89d2328ab9d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a9cd5f1-cfb7-5a25-b73f-89d2328ab9d4" "answer-665a8330-259b-54cb-824e-dff4c4b69374" "answer-0ff3f3c4-60a4-5f30-a928-24d65afeda4a" "answer-fdb6008b-4190-517a-b2e2-2c5b4ac708ed" "answer-08f8b5c5-5a79-5789-bffa-95fbf9c0cca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a9cd5f1-cfb7-5a25-b73f-89d2328ab9d4" :answer/id #uuid "7a9cd5f1-cfb7-5a25-b73f-89d2328ab9d4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/24/24aae5c27fc48b7a340e36f6a54d9d6d636644c938e5328c1a8c68713179a947.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-665a8330-259b-54cb-824e-dff4c4b69374" :answer/id #uuid "665a8330-259b-54cb-824e-dff4c4b69374" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5a/5a4e843aecb4855baad729fc9c1864ae19ab95733bd89396605a9544b241258f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ff3f3c4-60a4-5f30-a928-24d65afeda4a" :answer/id #uuid "0ff3f3c4-60a4-5f30-a928-24d65afeda4a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7f/7f2bd4a766b0acd0ddfa4c613b8b145cfc1065c2bd68bd4225262c998cd85f3a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdb6008b-4190-517a-b2e2-2c5b4ac708ed" :answer/id #uuid "fdb6008b-4190-517a-b2e2-2c5b4ac708ed" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a4/a44c42c06b2dd3c2465910498ea1f74632f1adc85b23d527e9596e73499f8d23.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08f8b5c5-5a79-5789-bffa-95fbf9c0cca6" :answer/id #uuid "08f8b5c5-5a79-5789-bffa-95fbf9c0cca6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c9/c956047bf140923ce38416d6f70374c94c37ae1c067584ced3ba4c831f036360.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055952 :tutorial/content "Consider the graph of the parabola ![](images/f2/f218c572691a74963cd3808bf4df2923122e84b65d1fabf1138bab6264b043b5.svg) shown below.\n\n![](images/45/450251899f728a3cc927b72fdb7655204828c8e0be0432cb08cee2462d6e5bfe.png)\n\nWe can describe many features of the graph using mathematical terminology:\n\n- The ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-intercepts of the parabola are at ![](images/81/8171bb8403bd612f56ef5f32f400f1aef8efeed51ea279d36779771fdea1ae0d.svg) and ![](images/77/779cec712506e0f798805963ab85841b46650fb22681d97a64aec4b85a47d07f.svg) We say that ![](images/b0/b064281df4bef2506521322c7477468b9cc565616e2c5b6f21000df6522399c1.svg) and ![](images/1f/1fb9f2f73a09599931892c1dee7629975b4d851e5dd6f0d07b7c641bbf17bf54.svg) are the **roots** (or **zeros**) of the parabola.\n\n- The parabola intersects the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis at  ![](images/6a/6a0e2cbf9f56c3c989ad96f020fe8bb0f7c785ff6de8073c476232b95476ac13.svg). We say that ![](images/78/78d4465d85b55cee3832a9b598a2564b6a3fa9a072de8a1fb4b40ca884079670.svg) is the **![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercept**. The ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercept is the same as the constant term of the function.\n\n- The parabola has a \"turning point\" at  ![](images/ef/ef43561f9d825c9e79fb03dffafa744d386d0c2a5a07da903675bca120d59fd1.svg) which is called the **vertex**. In an upwards parabola (like the one shown above), the vertex is the minimum point, while in a downwards parabola, the vertex is the maximum point.\n\n- The vertical line  ![](images/df/df9822243c11ec9f0fabca5cc578976d0bdea2c521b4f61964f5f3850a970504.svg) that passes through the vertex is called the **axis of symmetry**. The part of the parabola to the left of the axis of symmetry is the mirror image of the right, and vice versa.\n\n- This particular parabola is **upward opening** because it has a distinctive ![](images/13/13ab0b72e7963f3e74404b8b75f12654ece94c2c44e1fb09fdf230b976eb681b.svg) shape. A parabola ![](images/7c/7c49eede8f0eb80dadd8384ae942dc8248ef454eeb6afa1aeba7ae48e7545456.svg) is upward opening if the quadratic coefficient is positive ![](images/d2/d2a0fc4d90b45e06999c89b1a40ff6f01116e9c429c195adbfced573f9e47660.svg)\n\n- Parabolas can also be **downward opening** with a distinctive ![](images/57/57872695daf3067460adec5a506cfb1457729de4eeac879eab9f7355570bac11.svg) shape. A parabola ![](images/7c/7c49eede8f0eb80dadd8384ae942dc8248ef454eeb6afa1aeba7ae48e7545456.svg) is downward opening if the quadratic coefficient is negative ![](images/a1/a16d199f292dbd74941402b3d485cf107a7a985d28aeb13ab50ff6baf87f2d4b.svg)\n\nLet's take a look at an example of a downward opening parabola." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054926 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186195013 :answer-field/choices 17592186195016] [:db/retract 17592186195013 :answer-field/choices 17592186195014] [:db/retract 17592186195013 :answer-field/choices 17592186195015] [:db/retract 17592186195006 :answer-field/choices 17592186195008] [:db/retract 17592186195006 :answer-field/choices 17592186195009] [:db/retract 17592186195006 :answer-field/choices 17592186195007] {:db/id 17592186198256 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e78ca7a7-d4e4-5c94-b10c-7178217e2c2b" "question-12705253-40c6-5f3d-bde2-d9b9b3c2a300"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198257 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cd5faa7d-a0da-5855-abab-cb9f9cd47a6c" "question-16975edf-5610-5167-bf92-0dd71021b831" "question-af2842e6-dea4-50ab-b263-09b224915c23" "question-4e83f3e0-1564-59fb-a764-5da5f052add0" "question-1e781df2-007a-5016-ba10-713cbfb69f20"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198258 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a6263d9-7a39-5199-9f93-7ac1161cd5e5" "question-fbeaf179-7e47-5b15-8eb5-f5fa351b4082" "question-502d8fb9-af55-51a0-accb-d73687bf175c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e78ca7a7-d4e4-5c94-b10c-7178217e2c2b" :question/id #uuid "e78ca7a7-d4e4-5c94-b10c-7178217e2c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-183280" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is not an even integer, and $x$ divides $50.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is an even integer\n\n- $D(x):$ $x$ divides $50$" :question/worked-solution "The sentence \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not an even integer.\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬C.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\n¬C∧D.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e06897d1-a528-57ed-b458-505cba32da27"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e06897d1-a528-57ed-b458-505cba32da27" :answer-field/id #uuid "e06897d1-a528-57ed-b458-505cba32da27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e88b4693-6835-565d-8cbf-5b716da17401" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7981a515-a643-55bc-b99a-908835ca98b9" "answer-e8df6388-82d4-50b5-813f-c9893e93776a" "answer-e88b4693-6835-565d-8cbf-5b716da17401" "answer-2cb0bfe1-2fd3-5cf3-824c-34246fea8c8f" "answer-d3055cf3-8f86-5a91-a4c3-c8d13469f8b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7981a515-a643-55bc-b99a-908835ca98b9" :answer/id #uuid "7981a515-a643-55bc-b99a-908835ca98b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C∨¬D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8df6388-82d4-50b5-813f-c9893e93776a" :answer/id #uuid "e8df6388-82d4-50b5-813f-c9893e93776a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬(C∧D)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e88b4693-6835-565d-8cbf-5b716da17401" :answer/id #uuid "e88b4693-6835-565d-8cbf-5b716da17401" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬C∧D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cb0bfe1-2fd3-5cf3-824c-34246fea8c8f" :answer/id #uuid "2cb0bfe1-2fd3-5cf3-824c-34246fea8c8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬C∧¬D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3055cf3-8f86-5a91-a4c3-c8d13469f8b9" :answer/id #uuid "d3055cf3-8f86-5a91-a4c3-c8d13469f8b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬C∨D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198695 :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is neither irrational nor complex.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $S(x):$ $x$ is irrational\n\n- $T(x):$ $x$ is complex" :question/worked-solution "The given sentence is equivalent to the following sentence: \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not irrational, and $x$ is not complex.\n\nLet's break our sentence down into individual statements:\n\n- The statement \"$x$ is not irrational\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬S.$\n\n- The statement \"$x$ is not complex\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬T.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n\n$$\n¬S∧¬T.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194796 :answer-field/correct 17592186194797 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-12705253-40c6-5f3d-bde2-d9b9b3c2a300" :question/id #uuid "12705253-40c6-5f3d-bde2-d9b9b3c2a300" :question/math-academy-id "q-183269" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$ is not both a multiple of $5$ and a multiple of $9.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $9$" :question/worked-solution "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is both a multiple of $5$ and a multiple of $9.$\n\nThe sentence above can be expressed symbolically as $P∧Q,$ and we can negate this sentence using the symbol \"$¬$\".\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n\n$$\n¬(P∧Q).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c1655ff9-41d1-5d75-8e39-7f09e632c123"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c1655ff9-41d1-5d75-8e39-7f09e632c123" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1655ff9-41d1-5d75-8e39-7f09e632c123" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e709e59-fc9b-581a-9a73-d928809c39b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e6fc7a57-5c7e-5edc-a302-39b709d7283c" "answer-0e709e59-fc9b-581a-9a73-d928809c39b8" "answer-01c43c1c-f187-5d74-8aed-81f34a717110" "answer-bf3adcd5-7b76-552c-9ca5-e6e32e82024c" "answer-7c0da829-aa4d-5367-b177-bd093d8b5659"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6fc7a57-5c7e-5edc-a302-39b709d7283c" :answer/id #uuid "e6fc7a57-5c7e-5edc-a302-39b709d7283c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e709e59-fc9b-581a-9a73-d928809c39b8" :answer/id #uuid "0e709e59-fc9b-581a-9a73-d928809c39b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬(P∧Q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01c43c1c-f187-5d74-8aed-81f34a717110" :answer/id #uuid "01c43c1c-f187-5d74-8aed-81f34a717110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬(P∨Q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf3adcd5-7b76-552c-9ca5-e6e32e82024c" :answer/id #uuid "bf3adcd5-7b76-552c-9ca5-e6e32e82024c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬(P∨¬Q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c0da829-aa4d-5367-b177-bd093d8b5659" :answer/id #uuid "7c0da829-aa4d-5367-b177-bd093d8b5659" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∧Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd5faa7d-a0da-5855-abab-cb9f9cd47a6c" :question/id #uuid "cd5faa7d-a0da-5855-abab-cb9f9cd47a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183283" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x$  is even and $y$ is prime.\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$  is even and $y$ is prime\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x\\text{ is even and }y\\text{ is prime}) & ≡¬(x\\text{ is even}∧y\\text{ is prime}) \\\\  & ≡¬(x\\text{ is even})∨¬(y\\text{ is prime}) \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is odd}∨y\\text{ is not prime} \\\\  & ≡x\\text{ is odd or }y\\text{ is not prime}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70ff9543-4a2f-55fa-90aa-717f4aadaaf1" "answer-field-205fa214-ed71-5647-8d55-dbce11fd1905" "answer-field-093a30ee-c73e-55fe-adc9-bfeaf2ca05b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70ff9543-4a2f-55fa-90aa-717f4aadaaf1" :answer-field/id #uuid "70ff9543-4a2f-55fa-90aa-717f4aadaaf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8504797e-9e04-5eaa-879c-9a80a0f6eec2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b7ec1376-c18c-50a4-83a0-ab9adbf4bed3" "answer-8504797e-9e04-5eaa-879c-9a80a0f6eec2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7ec1376-c18c-50a4-83a