answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9586b5e-6b6a-5eb0-8d9c-fb74207d48ee" :answer/id #uuid "a9586b5e-6b6a-5eb0-8d9c-fb74207d48ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092761 :question/problem "Given that ${a}_{1}=-18$ and $\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-0.9$ for all integers $n\\ge 1,$ find the value of ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given series is geometric series because the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nWe're told that the first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=-18.\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-0.9.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18}{1-(-0.9)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{1+0.9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{1.9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{180}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186090766 :answer-field/correct 17592186090769 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233350 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3091e31c-4430-5ffe-b4b7-0a02be1e4edf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3091e31c-4430-5ffe-b4b7-0a02be1e4edf" :answer-field/id #uuid "3091e31c-4430-5ffe-b4b7-0a02be1e4edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb0d9032-620e-5573-8ccc-ca1cd595057d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-631ca0b5-ae05-5843-8fce-eaa43004c3a3" "answer-14bf80a3-1665-5977-9753-8899ce180734" "answer-8fbbebd6-1052-5e30-bf33-b4a804d2efb5" "answer-e9c2927b-5f83-5559-9be7-b5aabb0973ee" "answer-fb0d9032-620e-5573-8ccc-ca1cd595057d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/v