{1.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-92506140-a021-54d4-9afc-c6047e832c6b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-92506140-a021-54d4-9afc-c6047e832c6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "92506140-a021-54d4-9afc-c6047e832c6b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-03fb69b0-fb4a-5df6-aac8-69f15b52ee53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03fb69b0-fb4a-5df6-aac8-69f15b52ee53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03fb69b0-fb4a-5df6-aac8-69f15b52ee53" :answer/id #uuid "03fb69b0-fb4a-5df6-aac8-69f15b52ee53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fbd76d75-8ee7-5bcd-acb2-1f5ae9aa3787" :question/id #uuid "fbd76d75-8ee7-5bcd-acb2-1f5ae9aa3787" :question/math-academy-id "q-67301" :question/problem "${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{n}=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given series is a geometric series because it is in the form $\\sum a{r}^{n}.$ \n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nThe first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=8{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}=6.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{8{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}}{8{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(1-\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d3c44b61-550f-50e7-828e-641fd371090c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3c44b61-550f-50e7-828e-641fd371