94758f1a2164" :question/id #uuid "858e5587-42fe-5f2f-94b7-94758f1a2164" :question/math-academy-id "q-348315" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f33fde62793530cfe8970a9fea690fc71036312483ea617088a8d0a663d5133a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =(\\theta +\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-451b0468-1ab6-5622-abf5-d01927a565b8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-451b0468-1ab6-5622-abf5-d01927a565b8" :answer-field/id #uuid "451b0468-1ab6-5622-abf5-d01927a565b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f1ffe733-727d-5ca8-9de6-2f0a4144bd80" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1ffe733-727d-5ca8-9de6-2f0a4144bd80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1ffe733-727d-5ca8-9de6-2f0a4144bd80" :answer/id #uuid "f1ffe733-727d-5ca8-9de6-2f0a4144bd80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-86ea583e-6e3e-5bb4-93ab-14ccfe18681c" :question/id #uuid "86ea583e-6e3e-5bb4-93ab-14ccfe18681c" :question/math-academy-id "q-352297" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi +0 \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d7cde26-15d1-5ea3-9851-e82954572829"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d7cde26-15d1-5ea3-9851-e82954572829" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7cde26-15d1-5ea3-9851-e82954572829" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b0b39530-de5a-5c77-986a-201fc9682d01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0b39530-de5a-5c77-986a-201fc9682d01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0b39530-de5a-5c77-986a-201fc9682d01" :answer/id #uuid "b0b39530-de5a-5c77-986a-201fc9682d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c7bf914-2de6-57ee-85dd-b40dcc8d6cfc" :question/id #uuid "3c7bf914-2de6-57ee-85dd-b40dcc8d6cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-9640" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7ca646111a7708da96fa1bea8aca056abf0c45f9a4295e2beb27181d704aa814.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{8},$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a913a76-11e5-57cb-aec7-0eda0a258d42"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a913a76-11e5-57cb-aec7-0eda0a258d42" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a913a76-11e5-57cb-aec7-0eda0a258d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4c18dc99-1f3e-572b-b474-4613ba1ccc54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41ba3cc1-a57c-5405-a9a7-4fc4022e386b" "answer-01e8e637-7057-5738-bf7e-37e493294f83" "answer-15e653f1-5de1-53ea-abbc-55ef743af9eb" "answer-4c18dc99-1f3e-572b-b474-4613ba1ccc54" "answer-ba5b425b-9a81-5998-a220-805626423f1b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ba3cc1-a57c-5405-a9a7-4fc4022e386b" :answer/id #uuid "41ba3cc1-a57c-5405-a9a7-4fc4022e386b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01e8e637-7057-5738-bf7e-37e493294f83" :answer/id #uuid "01e8e637-7057-5738-bf7e-37e493294f83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15e653f1-5de1-53ea-abbc-55ef743af9eb" :answer/id #uuid "15e653f1-5de1-53ea-abbc-55ef743af9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c18dc99-1f3e-572b-b474-4613ba1ccc54" :answer/id #uuid "4c18dc99-1f3e-572b-b474-4613ba1ccc54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba5b425b-9a81-5998-a220-805626423f1b" :answer/id #uuid "ba5b425b-9a81-5998-a220-805626423f1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-85d4b81f-f257-5ee9-9249-f54ff8b0fda6" :question/id #uuid "85d4b81f-f257-5ee9-9249-f54ff8b0fda6" :question/math-academy-id "q-352298" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =2\\pi +0 \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5704968-f186-54d5-a951-55effb0d3ff9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5704968-f186-54d5-a951-55effb0d3ff9" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5704968-f186-54d5-a951-55effb0d3ff9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cf4aa39e-778f-58ff-8308-65c8627a83b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cf4aa39e-778f-58ff-8308-65c8627a83b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf4aa39e-778f-58ff-8308-65c8627a83b5" :answer/id #uuid "cf4aa39e-778f-58ff-8308-65c8627a83b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-529c609b-d364-5c28-a5a9-2026822f240a" :question/id #uuid "529c609b-d364-5c28-a5a9-2026822f240a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79626" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the area bounded by graph of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb2074a7-cded-5820-bd6c-23291aa6aaef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb2074a7-cded-5820-bd6c-23291aa6aaef" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb2074a7-cded-5820-bd6c-23291aa6aaef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a62d9ca-70cf-5bb0-a81d-b44818d65dcd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-604b5f92-c114-511e-a74d-0dc1e2510766" "answer-3baf6327-0772-5626-bef1-153ab2509f41" "answer-d575583a-8ede-5730-b7c0-283f632cd4e2" "answer-2a62d9ca-70cf-5bb0-a81d-b44818d65dcd" "answer-d9f01578-2351-567b-8c59-f1220aaa327e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-604b5f92-c114-511e-a74d-0dc1e2510766" :answer/id #uuid "604b5f92-c114-511e-a74d-0dc1e2510766" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3baf6327-0772-5626-bef1-153ab2509f41" :answer/id #uuid "3baf6327-0772-5626-bef1-153ab2509f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d575583a-8ede-5730-b7c0-283f632cd4e2" :answer/id #uuid "d575583a-8ede-5730-b7c0-283f632cd4e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a62d9ca-70cf-5bb0-a81d-b44818d65dcd" :answer/id #uuid "2a62d9ca-70cf-5bb0-a81d-b44818d65dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9f01578-2351-567b-8c59-f1220aaa327e" :answer/id #uuid "d9f01578-2351-567b-8c59-f1220aaa327e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-acc4627b-a75b-5710-8130-818c19bd3eef" :question/id #uuid "acc4627b-a75b-5710-8130-818c19bd3eef" :question/math-academy-id "q-352321" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}(3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}(9+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}(9+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +8(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(17\\theta +24\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(17\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+24\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+12(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}))+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{3}+12(\\sqrt{3})+2(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{3}+14\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea42cbea-59a6-5df3-b3cd-da64d32d78f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea42cbea-59a6-5df3-b3cd-da64d32d78f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea42cbea-59a6-5df3-b3cd-da64d32d78f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e0fa857c-1d3e-5cf2-baa1-2ef2c08c36f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e0fa857c-1d3e-5cf2-baa1-2ef2c08c36f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0fa857c-1d3e-5cf2-baa1-2ef2c08c36f7" :answer/id #uuid "e0fa857c-1d3e-5cf2-baa1-2ef2c08c36f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{3}+14\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9bf3624-c382-5070-9fe1-d9a42b576ac0" :question/id #uuid "d9bf3624-c382-5070-9fe1-d9a42b576ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-79793" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the total area enclosed by the graph of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\,$ for $\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a7f30de-c83e-5e20-b1c0-29f77397e42d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a7f30de-c83e-5e20-b1c0-29f77397e42d" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a7f30de-c83e-5e20-b1c0-29f77397e42d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b065bdc2-bb70-5ec7-bdfa-649ce2e20ba5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b309ec04-8226-537c-b8f0-96608e7c2284" "answer-3d1413a7-a029-529d-a86f-b8d38b5b7dff" "answer-2a9f0a47-5957-5b08-aa87-f0e9f9dae695" "answer-690e9529-0386-51ce-be2d-a3189387b6fc" "answer-b065bdc2-bb70-5ec7-bdfa-649ce2e20ba5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b309ec04-8226-537c-b8f0-96608e7c2284" :answer/id #uuid "b309ec04-8226-537c-b8f0-96608e7c2284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d1413a7-a029-529d-a86f-b8d38b5b7dff" :answer/id #uuid "3d1413a7-a029-529d-a86f-b8d38b5b7dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a9f0a47-5957-5b08-aa87-f0e9f9dae695" :answer/id #uuid "2a9f0a47-5957-5b08-aa87-f0e9f9dae695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-690e9529-0386-51ce-be2d-a3189387b6fc" :answer/id #uuid "690e9529-0386-51ce-be2d-a3189387b6fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b065bdc2-bb70-5ec7-bdfa-649ce2e20ba5" :answer/id #uuid "b065bdc2-bb70-5ec7-bdfa-649ce2e20ba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092628 :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a83949bcdf4ed8d99cac451d6db21986c24819d1601578890f86fe3df99666a.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(4+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi })) \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =3\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =3(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-4+\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -8}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186090051 :answer-field/correct "answer-6b4da550-43d1-5bf0-ba07-2d9c8866fa45" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a23714c3-4f78-5ba1-a107-d1e73692eea4" "answer-87cb5c61-72c1-5207-ac68-6c4fc40a404e" "answer-9c7ba2fb-9f38-56bc-8fe5-e96e6dbabc3b" "answer-6b4da550-43d1-5bf0-ba07-2d9c8866fa45" "answer-f974103f-b624-52cf-acc4-f3366c464e19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a23714c3-4f78-5ba1-a107-d1e73692eea4" :answer/id #uuid "a23714c3-4f78-5ba1-a107-d1e73692eea4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +4}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87cb5c61-72c1-5207-ac68-6c4fc40a404e" :answer/id #uuid "87cb5c61-72c1-5207-ac68-6c4fc40a404e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +8}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c7ba2fb-9f38-56bc-8fe5-e96e6dbabc3b" :answer/id #uuid "9c7ba2fb-9f38-56bc-8fe5-e96e6dbabc3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +8}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b4da550-43d1-5bf0-ba07-2d9c8866fa45" :answer/id #uuid "6b4da550-43d1-5bf0-ba07-2d9c8866fa45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi -8}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f974103f-b624-52cf-acc4-f3366c464e19" :answer/id #uuid "f974103f-b624-52cf-acc4-f3366c464e19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-692ede8e-6241-512f-89fd-e5f23e8be1b4" :question/id #uuid "692ede8e-6241-512f-89fd-e5f23e8be1b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-9641" :question/problem "![](images/ed/ed702f9d982d599fc0f175dc7d7dd022aeefc3f5463aade2a9db71313faf4866.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi })) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\pi -0)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)+\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0+\\frac{1}{8}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4863b9c5-7c52-590c-ac4a-f95a2e691add"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4863b9c5-7c52-590c-ac4a-f95a2e691add" :answer-field/id #uuid "4863b9c5-7c52-590c-ac4a-f95a2e691add" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1e72018-e6e3-592b-880f-a6d48f3ebdb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-771fcce6-ddaf-54b3-a739-a6390529f5f8" "answer-b1e72018-e6e3-592b-880f-a6d48f3ebdb7" "answer-460f98e6-2dad-5164-97ed-ca84fd3c06be" "answer-b294df79-b64d-5dcb-8a58-b77dd62b8429" "answer-e6233b81-6983-586a-81cd-f71c40f0288b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-771fcce6-ddaf-54b3-a739-a6390529f5f8" :answer/id #uuid "771fcce6-ddaf-54b3-a739-a6390529f5f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e72018-e6e3-592b-880f-a6d48f3ebdb7" :answer/id #uuid "b1e72018-e6e3-592b-880f-a6d48f3ebdb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-460f98e6-2dad-5164-97ed-ca84fd3c06be" :answer/id #uuid "460f98e6-2dad-5164-97ed-ca84fd3c06be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b294df79-b64d-5dcb-8a58-b77dd62b8429" :answer/id #uuid "b294df79-b64d-5dcb-8a58-b77dd62b8429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6233b81-6983-586a-81cd-f71c40f0288b" :answer/id #uuid "e6233b81-6983-586a-81cd-f71c40f0288b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c3c2375-fac6-5465-bbbf-42c39eaebb70" :question/id #uuid "3c3c2375-fac6-5465-bbbf-42c39eaebb70" :question/math-academy-id "q-123912" :question/problem "![](images/98/98bc6f2ea4d71368226f0f784d629e98949e07005bc08158206de35a87bea520.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=2\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(9-18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi })) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{8}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}(2\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-9(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{8}-9+\\frac{9}{8}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi -72}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-870af8e4-9463-5142-8458-8ef364ddaa4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-870af8e4-9463-5142-8458-8ef364ddaa4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "870af8e4-9463-5142-8458-8ef364ddaa4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1addd5e-b739-5991-8970-6b78acd4e746" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b1addd5e-b739-5991-8970-6b78acd4e746" "answer-a5649c91-b6ce-5e11-a61e-4473ca3b44bf" "answer-773ffc42-e2cb-572a-9030-e9a10ba881ba" "answer-a8b16dc0-ef14-5998-aff3-022fa9ad94bd" "answer-a1bcdf62-382b-5121-8803-109ccdad8245"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1addd5e-b739-5991-8970-6b78acd4e746" :answer/id #uuid "b1addd5e-b739-5991-8970-6b78acd4e746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi -72}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5649c91-b6ce-5e11-a61e-4473ca3b44bf" :answer/id #uuid "a5649c91-b6ce-5e11-a61e-4473ca3b44bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi -9}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-773ffc42-e2cb-572a-9030-e9a10ba881ba" :answer/id #uuid "773ffc42-e2cb-572a-9030-e9a10ba881ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi +24}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8b16dc0-ef14-5998-aff3-022fa9ad94bd" :answer/id #uuid "a8b16dc0-ef14-5998-aff3-022fa9ad94bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi +72}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1bcdf62-382b-5121-8803-109ccdad8245" :answer/id #uuid "a1bcdf62-382b-5121-8803-109ccdad8245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186320607 :answer-field/correct "answer-04429390-e74b-5e41-90c1-15316c84504e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04429390-e74b-5e41-90c1-15316c84504e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04429390-e74b-5e41-90c1-15316c84504e" :answer/id #uuid "04429390-e74b-5e41-90c1-15316c84504e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^3}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d870d48d-9aa5-5918-85fa-03f4b0df3775" :question/id #uuid "d870d48d-9aa5-5918-85fa-03f4b0df3775" :question/math-academy-id "q-352336" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\theta }^{3}}{3}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3})-2(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-55196b73-4bdb-541d-9f20-8e0ffb0bc727"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-55196b73-4bdb-541d-9f20-8e0ffb0bc727" :answer-field/id #uuid "55196b73-4bdb-541d-9f20-8e0ffb0bc727" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c83586b2-1d92-5d5e-8f6e-4972aca897e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c83586b2-1d92-5d5e-8f6e-4972aca897e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c83586b2-1d92-5d5e-8f6e-4972aca897e1" :answer/id #uuid "c83586b2-1d92-5d5e-8f6e-4972aca897e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2437a359-bd35-5179-92d6-ee80bc33d39e" :question/id #uuid "2437a359-bd35-5179-92d6-ee80bc33d39e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124357" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the total area enclosed by graph of the polar curve $r=9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b58951d-0e27-5ba8-8189-e5a72fc144d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b58951d-0e27-5ba8-8189-e5a72fc144d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b58951d-0e27-5ba8-8189-e5a72fc144d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-380fba56-3bbd-5139-8fa0-4225147239fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-380fba56-3bbd-5139-8fa0-4225147239fd" "answer-9440c8ed-7f27-549a-8592-91eb673a829c" "answer-20a4bb8c-88f1-5914-b2d5-3312538c815e" "answer-c3e81b37-5a0d-5f3a-a5d2-b8283486c586" "answer-32de64f9-d1f2-5273-a235-791a355a3cda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-380fba56-3bbd-5139-8fa0-4225147239fd" :answer/id #uuid "380fba56-3bbd-5139-8fa0-4225147239fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9440c8ed-7f27-549a-8592-91eb673a829c" :answer/id #uuid "9440c8ed-7f27-549a-8592-91eb673a829c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20a4bb8c-88f1-5914-b2d5-3312538c815e" :answer/id #uuid "20a4bb8c-88f1-5914-b2d5-3312538c815e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(3\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3e81b37-5a0d-5f3a-a5d2-b8283486c586" :answer/id #uuid "c3e81b37-5a0d-5f3a-a5d2-b8283486c586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5\\theta -9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32de64f9-d1f2-5273-a235-791a355a3cda" :answer/id #uuid "32de64f9-d1f2-5273-a235-791a355a3cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ba92fa4-3450-58d7-9f90-59493b716e4d" :question/id #uuid "2ba92fa4-3450-58d7-9f90-59493b716e4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352331" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3f2350ba3651e928c65e1a78908a8f8e93cb690585a3fa16b723d1cf38a5024.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )}{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{9}{2}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9}{2}\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )}{8}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+4) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{9\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f185ea2-90bf-5f97-91ff-946b826ac36e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f185ea2-90bf-5f97-91ff-946b826ac36e" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f185ea2-90bf-5f97-91ff-946b826ac36e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-33c8c1d5-6245-5e5d-af86-ae89e6d91c80" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33c8c1d5-6245-5e5d-af86-ae89e6d91c80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33c8c1d5-6245-5e5d-af86-ae89e6d91c80" :answer/id #uuid "33c8c1d5-6245-5e5d-af86-ae89e6d91c80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+\\frac{9\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-63188c95-9ec2-54ce-9302-58600c7d5645" :question/id #uuid "63188c95-9ec2-54ce-9302-58600c7d5645" :question/math-academy-id "q-352326" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7ab46adacda52da11a07c783905161c6a6c8ebadb77423d7c70acdb17321a50e.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+5{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+\\frac{5(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))}{2}+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{13}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{13}{2}\\theta -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{13\\pi }{4}+6) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{13\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pi +24}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2b1fe94c-bcca-5ef1-b698-9fc1476d4a23"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b1fe94c-bcca-5ef1-b698-9fc1476d4a23" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1fe94c-bcca-5ef1-b698-9fc1476d4a23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-622acefd-6fc4-5289-acf9-eacb640ce3ef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-622acefd-6fc4-5289-acf9-eacb640ce3ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-622acefd-6fc4-5289-acf9-eacb640ce3ef" :answer/id #uuid "622acefd-6fc4-5289-acf9-eacb640ce3ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093357 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find the area of the region bounded by the polar curve $r = 3\\cos\\theta$ and the rays $\\theta_1 = 0$ and $\\theta_2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ as shown in blue in the picture below. Can we calculate this area using polar coordinates?\n\n![](images/2c/2c7e638a338aed2155ef5bf388be1f83a3a67d2296d5be09987b099a07edacbd.png)\n\nIn general, the area of the region bounded by a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ and the rays $\\theta=\\theta_1$ and $\\theta=\\theta_2$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2 \\:\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the half-circle above can be obtained as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\theta {|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093452 :tutorial/content "We've been using the following formula for the area of the region bounded by a polar curve ![](images/70/7031a0f3ab71df36bc36e925fcf4f04dbfc4feec5f374092855ef8d97b104452.svg) and the rays ![](images/38/38b971de9610efe2ed0de9f10956c73cf5cd967a86a5bcbb076791f369c22bef.svg) and ![](images/81/818e2605a585628c4becd20664b58007dbd2348ca664c80be6a838868a64693a.svg)\n\n![](images/55/55ffcf934c3a9e33a3376fa1796e6fb68ad1198d719db5ea094fe8eb46c5f47d.svg)\n\nBut where does this formula come from?\n\nTo see where the formula comes from, we can think about breaking up the area bounded by a polar curve into infinitesimally small sectors of circles.\n\nAs shown in the graph below, each sector has a radius of ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) and spans an infinitesimally small angle, ![](images/09/0904a69fa5e6a3a10eaf74b3fdd865db92761eeeffffae1c0badd33ffdf5b34b.svg)\n\n![](images/82/82be86e7092a97ca5b2f1423f32b15030af0c8c63bf47ece8be40b45720ac905.png)\n\nThe ratio of the area of a sector to the full area of the circle must be the same as the ratio of the angle of the sector to a full revolution of the circle. So, if the area of a sector is ![](images/0b/0b2376d17b173024d6f6c82faaff585293e9830ba7ce0764ecf8338adcd14994.svg) then we can set up and solve the following proportion:\n\n![](images/5d/5d318385ab16ee14d784b33c00180a44ade7cee2e97ffeafd290171d0d44868f.svg)\n\nFinally, to find the area under the curve, we can integrate the areas of all the sectors:\n\n![](images/a7/a75940f74a02ceadff519af028783a0e704fba8a73c4abf36c6a371deb56dee7.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092396 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093082 :step/math-academy-id 636917 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093083 :step/math-academy-id 636918 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093084 :step/math-academy-id 636921 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093127 :step/math-academy-id 636924 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186093145 :step/math-academy-id 636927 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
